# AIML Practical Work – Machine Learning & Data Visualization

## About This Repository

This repository contains my academic practical work as a B.Tech Computer Science Engineering student specializing in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning.

It includes implementations of Machine Learning algorithms and Data Visualization techniques using Python and Microsoft Power BI.

## Technologies & Tools Used

- Python
- Jupyter Notebook
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Scikit-learn
- Microsoft Power BI
- Power Query
- CSV Datasets

## 1. Machine Learning Practicals

The repository includes practical implementations of Machine Learning concepts and algorithms, such as:

- Simple Linear Regression
- Multiple Linear Regression
- Logistic Regression
- Regression with Regularization
- Principal Component Analysis (PCA)
- Support Vector Machine (SVM)
- Decision Tree Classification
- Naive Bayes Classifier
- K-Means Clustering

## 2. Data Visualization Practicals

The repository also includes Power BI practicals covering:

- Getting Started with Power BI
- Data Cleaning and Transformation
- Bar and Line Charts
- Interactive Dashboards with Filters and Slicers
- Geo-Visualization with Maps
- Pie and Donut Charts
- Heatmaps and Tree Maps
- Time Series Forecasting and Trend Lines

## Learning Objectives

- Understand and implement Machine Learning algorithms.
- Perform data preprocessing and analysis.
- Visualize data using charts and dashboards.
- Explore dimensionality reduction and clustering.
- Interpret model results and visualization insights.

